From d781fe1f4a392f4e9f82bc688c7a68b65ffd6e82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 11:22:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(design-system): add AleraStatusChip and AleraStatusBadge
 renderers

Patch 2 of the status badge standardization.

- Delete unused legacy lib/design_system/widgets/alera_status_badge.dart
  (a pill-shaped chip under the AleraStatusBadge name, referenced nowhere)
  to free the name for the circular overlay primitive.
- AleraStatusChip: read-only pill (icon + label), small/medium size variants,
  labelOverride, colours resolved strictly from AleraStatusColors.of(context)
  by the descriptor's tone. For single-patient views where identity is
  already established by context.
- AleraStatusBadge: compact circular glyph-only indicator on a solid,
  saturated tone background (not the soft chip fill, for legibility over
  photos), configurable ringColor/ringWidth so it can sit on a patient photo
  without colour bleed. Label still required as the accessible name since
  there is no visible text. Foundational primitive for AleraBadgedAvatar
  (Patch 3).
- Export both from status.dart alongside the Patch 1 foundation.
- Apply the reported feature/vital-trends-ui fix for the ThemeExtension
  type-bound error in AleraTheme.caregiver (list build + add, no spread).
- Tests: label/glyph rendering, labelOverride (visible text vs accessible
  name), merged semantics, light/dark colour resolution, chip size metrics,
  badge solid-vs-soft fill, ring colour/width incl. surface default, diameter
  -> icon size scaling.
